{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.SpinInvolutionLpDualInvariance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.SpinInvolutionLpDualInvariance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.mirror_nucleus_trace_equality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.mirror_nucleus_trace_equality","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance.lean#L269-L291","doc":"**Mirror-nucleus Markov-trace equality.**  For magic-shell\ncomposite operators `σ_pp` (Z=2 shell) and `σ_nn` (N=2 shell)\nthat are S-conjugate (`σ(σ_pp) = σ_nn`, expressing the\nHopf-antipode permutation of proton-shell ↔ neutron-shell\nstrand labels), the canonical Markov trace is equal:\n\n  τ(σ_pp) = τ(σ_nn).\n\nThis is the load-bearing positive finding (2) from the PR\n#638 closure work: AME data confirms this symmetry directly\n(substrate-binding difference between ³He and ³H vanishes\nafter Coulomb correction, to ~0.03 MeV ≈ 0.5%). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.pair_knot_Z_N_trace_invariance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.pair_knot_Z_N_trace_invariance","kind":"theorem","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance.lean#L250-L267","doc":"**Pair-knot Z↔N corollary.**  For any element `a` of a\nFrobenius algebra with spin involution `S`,\n`τ(S.sigma a) = τ(a)`.\n\nApplied at `a = σ_pp` (proton-pair sub-braid of magic-shell\natoms ³He, ⁴He), gives `τ(σ_pp) = τ(σ_nn)` where σ_nn is the\nneutron-pair sub-braid (Z↔N image of σ_pp under S = Hopf\nantipode permuting strand labels).\n\nThis is the **algebraic basis** for the `z_n_symmetry` axiom\nin `conj:magic-shell-stabilization`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.isospin_is_spin_grading_under_spin_involution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.isospin_is_spin_grading_under_spin_involution","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance.lean#L221-L235","doc":"Mathematical content of \"isospin\".  Isospin is the Z/2\ngrading attached to ANY Frobenius algebra equipped with a\nspin involution.  Every element decomposes as a + a' with\na := (1/2)(x + σ x) the singlet projection and a' := (1/2)(x − σ x)\nthe doublet projection.  T_3 is read off the doublet sign.\n\nNote: this lemma is a structural statement about the σ-fixed\nsubalgebra; it does not depend on the LP context. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qou_isospin_invariance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qou_isospin_invariance","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance.lean#L200-L219","doc":"QOU instance: the Hopf antipode S on H_n(R, q) is a spin\ninvolution; the Murphy central element P_ℓ = e_ℓ(J_1,…,J_n)\nis σ-invariant.  Consequently, mirror nuclei\n(β_K(Z, N), β_K(N, Z)) — Markov-conjugate under S — have\nexactly equal LP-dual binding-energy shadow prices.\n\n  y_0*(Z, N) = y_0*(N, Z).\n\nThis is the QOU rephrasing of the classical isospin\ninvariance of nuclear binding energies.\n\nThe instance construction\n(`MarkovHeckeSpinInvolution : SpinInvolution (HeckeMarkov R q n)`)\nis conditional on the Mathlib formalisation of the Hopf\nantipode on H_n(R, q); we record the statement here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.spin_invariance_of_y0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.spin_invariance_of_y0","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance.lean#L174-L198","doc":"Step 5 (main theorem).  σ-invariance of the LP-dual\nshadow price y_0*:\n\n  y_0*(σ(β)) = y_0*(β).\n\nProof: Steps 1–4 establish that LP(β) and LP(σ(β)) have\nfeasible sets in σ-bijection and the same σ-invariant\nobjective.  Their primal optima coincide; by strong duality\n(qou:QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction\n+ standard LP regularity) the dual optima coincide.\n\nThe full Lean encoding of an LP with both primal and dual\noptima requires Mathlib's LP infrastructure (currently\nnascent); the structural lemmas above (Steps 1–3) are the\nself-contained content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.lp_isomorphism_sigma_bijective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.lp_isomorphism_sigma_bijective","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance.lean#L152-L172","doc":"Step 4.  σ is a BIJECTION on `A` (since σ ∘ σ = id),\nso it bijects the feasible set of LP(β) with that of LP(σ(β)).\nCombined with Steps 2 (cone is σ-stable) and 3 (objective is\nσ-invariant), this yields an isomorphism of the two LPs.\n\nStatement: σ is bijective on `A`.  The companion\n`spin_invariant_cost` (Step 3) gives the objective half;\n`spin_stabilises_constraints` (Step 2) gives the constraint\nhalf; together with this bijectivity they constitute the\nLP isomorphism. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.spin_invariant_cost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.spin_invariant_cost","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance.lean#L139-L150","doc":"Step 3.  σ-invariant cost is fixed by x ↦ σ(x):\n\nτ(c · σ(x)) = τ(σ(σ(c) · x)) = τ(σ(c · x)) = τ(c · x). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.spin_stabilises_constraints","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.spin_stabilises_constraints","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance.lean#L110-L137","doc":"Step 2.  A σ-stable channel set defines a σ-stable cone.\n\nStatement: if `Sigma ⊆ A` is σ-stable\n(`∀ s ∈ Sigma, σ(s) ∈ Sigma`), then the cone\n`{x : ∀ s ∈ Sigma, τ(s · x) ≥ 0}` is σ-stable.\n\nPredicate-level encoding (no order class on R needed for the\nstatement; the actual ≥ 0 condition is parameterised by an\narbitrary predicate `nonneg : R → Prop`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.spin_isometric_pairing'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.spin_isometric_pairing'","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance.lean#L103-L108","doc":"Step 1, restated on the library's Frobenius pairing\n`F.pairing a b = F.τ (a * b)`: σ is a `pairing`-isometry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.spin_isometric_pairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.spin_isometric_pairing","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance.lean#L88-L101","doc":"Step 1.  σ is an isometry of the Frobenius pairing\n⟨a, b⟩ := τ(ab):\n\n  ⟨σ(a), σ(b)⟩ = τ(σ(a)σ(b)) = τ(σ(ba)) = τ(ba) = ⟨b, a⟩\n              = ⟨a, b⟩ (cyclicity).\n\nConcrete proof using the structure-encoded properties. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolution.star_compatible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolution.star_compatible","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance.lean#L86-L86","doc":"σ commutes with ⋆: σ(a⋆) = σ(a)⋆. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolution.star_anti_multiplicative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolution.star_anti_multiplicative","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance.lean#L84-L84","doc":"(ab)⋆ = b⋆ a⋆. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolution.star_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolution.star_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance.lean#L82-L82","doc":"⋆ ∘ ⋆ = id. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolution.trace_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolution.trace_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance.lean#L80-L80","doc":"τ ∘ σ = τ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolution.anti_multiplicative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolution.anti_multiplicative","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance.lean#L78-L78","doc":"σ(ab) = σ(b) σ(a) — anti-multiplicative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolution.involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolution.involutive","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance.lean#L76-L76","doc":"σ ∘ σ = id. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolution.star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolution.star","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance.lean#L74-L74","doc":"The *-anti-automorphism on A. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolution.sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolution.sigma","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance.lean#L72-L72","doc":"The involution σ : A → A. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolution.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolution.mk","kind":"ctor","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance.lean#L70-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolution","kind":"structure","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance.lean#L59-L86","doc":"A spin involution on a Frobenius *-trace algebra.\n\nThe fields encode the actual mathematical properties (involution,\nanti-multiplicativity, trace-invariance, *-compatibility) — not\nvacuous `True` placeholders.\n\nThe carrier `A` is the parameter of the library structure\n`FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction A R`; its multiplication is\nthe ring multiplication `*` and its trace is `F.τ`.  The *-structure\n`star` is given as part of this structure (so the pair `(F, S)`\nconstitutes a Frobenius *-algebra with spin involution). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:spin-involution","label":"def:spin-involution","md":"quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/spin-involution.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}